COMMERCIAL S11 TIMER FUTURE-GATE DIAGNOSIS

Status: ROOT_CAUSE_CONFIRMED; NO_RUNTIME_MUTATION
Observed safe code: S11_TIMER_FUTURE_RUN_MISSING

The first S11 deployment attempt stopped during source preflight, before the
backup boundary and before any runtime mutation. Four calendar-based S9 timers
reported a future NextElapseUSecRealtime. The active/enabled S10 health timer
uses OnBootSec plus OnUnitActiveSec, was in waiting state, and had a future run
in systemctl list-timers and NextElapseUSecMonotonic, while its realtime field
was empty. The controller incorrectly required the realtime field alone.

Risk assessment:
- Changing the existing timer would introduce unnecessary runtime drift.
- Accepting any active/enabled timer without a future property would weaken the
  liveness gate.
- The bounded correction is to require at least one non-empty, non-n/a future
  property: NextElapseUSecRealtime or NextElapseUSecMonotonic.

Backup and rollback:
- No backup was created because no mutation was reached; source state remains
  unchanged.
- The existing backup-first boundary and non-destructive S11-to-S10.2F rollback
  remain unchanged.
- The immutable r1 tag is not moved. A reviewed canonical Control successor is
  frozen as r2 before any retry.

Validation contract:
- Shell syntax and the complete Control suite must pass.
- PR CI and a same-SHA Codex review must be green.
- The r2 annotated tag must bind the exact canonical Application and Control
  commits and trees.
- Runtime retry must still pass the complete preflight before backup or mutation.
